ur (Awe & Vance, 2014). Other issue that enforces collaboration of statisticians with other domain experts is poor quality in the reporting and performance of statistical analyses in researches. It is very common and not restricted to journals with low impact factors. Poorquality statistical analysis is even observed in journals with high impact factor (Norström, 2015). For more than three decades, methodological problems have been identified and despite attempts to address them, progress has fallen short of expectations (Norström, 2015). Moreover “A meta-analysis of 100 peer-reviewed journal articles that performed secondary analysis of data from nationally representative surveys with complex sample designs found 1100 instances in which analytic errors may have occurred, and in 616 instances, these errors were likely present. Of the articles reviewed, 28% did not mention weighting data, 40% did not mention accounting for complex sample design to properly estimate variance, 59% used improper language when discussing results in the text (e.g. estimates generalized to the “sample” as opposed to the “population”), and 79% did not use proper significance testing” (Ward, 2018). It necessitates for researchers to contact statisticians or data science experts for accurate statistical analysis and its reporting.


