1.1 Laboratory of Interdisciplinary Statistical Analysis-Lahore College for Women University (LISA-LCWU)
LISA-LCWU became transitional member on 12th February, 2020 with particular focus on the capacity building and training the future generation of women statisticians. Vision and mission of LISA-LCWU is in alignment of LISA 2020 vision and mission. LISA-LCWU was granted membership of LISA 2020 network on 20th May, 2020 and it was 15th lab in line that got full membership. Performance of LISA-LWU before sustainability experiment is given in (Table 1). LISA-LCWU got two grants for trainings and workshops ($1964 + $900) from International Statistical Institute (ISI) and World Bank (TFSCB) through LISA UCB. LISA-LCWU has organized 14 workshops and 2 seminars before sustainability experiment (Table 1). The satisfaction level reported through feedback received from the participants was much encouraging to make the LISA-LCWU sustainable. Majority reported either satisfied or very satisfied (Figs. 1 and 2). In addition, LISA-LCWU has organized one international webinar and one statistical data analysis consultancy event. It has also organized poster competition titled “Let the Data Speak” in collaboration with the Office of Research Innovations and Commercialization (ORIC), LCWU and 53 participants from LCWU presented their research work. Faculty of Statistics department, LCWU are providing their services to LISA-LCWU voluntarily as a resource person for trainings and collaborations.
2 Big Question! Is LISA-LCWU on Sustainable Path?
LISA-LCWU has no budgetary head or any financial support from the university. The coordinator of LISA-LCWU is working voluntarily for all activities carried under it which is an additional burden along with her regular duties. In such a scenario it cannot be claimed that LISA-LCWU is on a strong and sustainable path. The lab is in a struggling position to enter into a strong sustainable process.


