LISA-LCWU was already publicizing its activities by sharing flyers in the university’s official WhatsApp group. It extended by including groups outside the university like WhatsApp groups of Islamic Society of Statistical Sciences (ISOSS), Ravians Statistics Department (GCU Lahore) alumni group and other known personnel of Statistics community in Pakistan.
E-Newsletter
Permission for bi-annual E-Newsletter of Statistics department has been taken from Vice Chancellor, LCWU, in which activities of LISA-LCWU will be given substantial space. Permission has been granted in the end of January, 2022 so 1st E-newsletter has been launched in August, 2022 and shared extensively within and outside the university. It may attract more domain experts by sharing success stories of LISA-LCWU and help to reduce trust deficit between domain expert and collaborators. https://www.lcwu.edu.pk/images/2022/downloads/STATISTICSENEWS LETTER.pdf
3.2 Allocation of Necessary Infrastructure
LISA-LCWU has been allocated a room that serves as its office. The office is equipped with a nameplate that is placed outside the room. Additionally, volunteers are instructed to spend some time in the office. This has had a positive impact on the recognition and image of LISA-LCWU. It provides a platform that makes it easier for collaborators to access the organization’s office. This accessibility to the office creates more opportunities for networking and collaboration.
3.3 Reduce Work Burden by Sharing Workload
To alleviate the burden of the lab coordinator and expand activities, it is imperative to involve more students and faculty members as collaborators. At first, in 2020 and 2021, the lab coordinator had to initiate collaborations by herself since no faculty member was willing to take on additional workload. However, the coordinator then began involving other members from the Statistics department, not only to share responsibilities but also to train collaborators to ensure the sustainability of the lab. For the sustainability experiment, undergraduate and graduate students were motivated and now the team has grown to include 17 members.


