7.1 Expected Outcomes of Experiments
The number of workshop participants increased after effective publicity of LISALCWU. This increase in participation facilitated the opportunity for more individuals to learn valuable data analysis skills. Furthermore, the increased publicity also served as an effective tool to convince domain experts of the value LISALCWU could bring to their research. The engagement of additional collaborators allowed for the first-time to organize the statistical data analysis consultancy desk, in which data analysis problems of 38 domain experts were addressed within a limited timeframe. Additionally, LISA-LCWU was invited to set up a Statistical Data Analysis Consultancy Desk at Research-Fest 2022 organized by a medical institute, and LISA-Internees worked on 15 projects. The involvement of more collaborators also shared the workload of LISA-LCWU coordinators and expanded the activities of LISA-LCWU. This expansion provided the opportunity to train additional collaborators and make the cycle of the stat-lab sustainable. Although LISA-LCWU applied for approval to charge a fee for workshops, it has not been approved by the competent authority yet. However, the allocation of a room for an office has given LISA-LCWU independent recognition. Additionally, the signing of the Letter of Intent (LoI) between the Department of Statistics LCWU, Pakistan, and the Department of Applied Mathematics, CU Boulder, USA, strengthens the connection of LISA-LCWU with LISA, University of Colorado Boulder. This connection can be helpful for future joint ventures that support the sustainability of LISA-LCWU.
7.2 Unexpected Outcomes of Experiments
Non-approval of fee charging was unforeseen. When applied for approval of fee charging from university authorities, they thought it is leading towards commercialization. Response of relevant departments involved in approval was quite unexpected.
8 Lessons Learnt from Sustainability Experiment
The following are the key takeaways from the sustainability experiment:
• It is important to consistently prioritize publicity by enhancing the quality of the website and updating it frequently, as well as extensively sharing E-Newsletters. • Members of LISA-LCWU should be assigned responsibilities to attend domain experts in the office.


