9 Post Experiment: Strengths and Weaknesses of LISA-LCWU
Following strengths and weaknesses of LISA-LCWU have been observed after sustainability experiments.
9.1 Strengths
After conducting the experiment, the following three enhancements have been made to the previously described strengths of LISA-LCWU:
• Allocation of a furnished office space with a nameplate of LISA-LCWU outside: This means that the university now has a designated office space which is equipped with necessary furniture, and a nameplate is placed outside to indicate that it is the official office of LISA-LCWU. • Engagement of more students pursuing Bachelor’s and Master’s degrees in Statistics as volunteers to provide assistance: This indicates that the lab is now involving more students from Statistics programs to work as volunteers for LISALCWU. • Substantial sharing of workload of the LISA-LCWU coordinator due to the involvement of other members: This means that other members of LISA-LCWU are now taking on more responsibilities to share the workload of the coordinator, making it easier to manage and achieve lab’s goals.
9.2 Weaknesses
The major obstacle that LISA-LCWU is currently facing is the shortage of financial resources. Despite having made significant strides in expanding its activities and collaborations, the lack of funds has hindered the stats lab’s ability to sustain its efforts and reach its full potential. This constraint has restricted the implementation of critical projects that require funding, which could help LISA-LCWU to expand its activities, acquire new equipment, and hire more staff. Despite this limitation, LISALCWU has been able to develop strategies to overcome this hurdle, such as applying for grants and seeking support from potential partners. By securing funding, LISALCWU can continue to expand its activities, enhance its sustainability, and offer its services to a wider range of individuals and organizations.


