10 Conclusion
The establishment of a webpage, a proper office, an increased number of collaborators, and the signing of a LoI with CU Boulder, USA, and LCWU have placed LISA-LCWU on a sustainable path by establishing a positive reputation within the institute and by sharing the workload. However, the biggest hurdle for LISA-LCWU is the lack of funds, which is hindering its consistency in progress. Therefore, LISALCWU needs to generate funds for self-reliance to maintain its sustainable path.
11 Future Recommendations/Strategies to Make LISA-LCWU Stronger and more Sustainable
LISA-LCWU needs blood (financial support/ budget from university or funded projects) for its survival. Following strategies have been planned for fund generation.
• Need assessment survey has been conducted to strengthen the case of approval for token fee charging to domain experts/researchers who want to collaborate with LISA-LCWU or to those who attend workshops/trainings organized by LISA-LCWU. Findings of these survey can provide supportive data-based evidence for the need and sustainability of LISA-LCWU to share with higher authorities of university (Appendix 1 and 2). • Internship at LISA-LCWU: Devise some strategies to engage students of Statistics department within and outside LCWU to do their internship at LISA-LCWU. • To get approval to include course on collaboration as a part of curriculum of degree in statistics at graduate and post graduate level. A course on statistical collaboration of three credit hours will be co-opted from LISA, University of Colorado Boulder, USA. Under this course, BS Statistics student should collaborate on one LISA-LCWU project and MS Statistics student should have to collaborate on two LISA-LCWU projects. These projects will be part of evaluation of these courses.
