Preliminary Results Based on Need Assessment Survey of Statistical Data Analysis Consultancy Center
During the sustainability experiment, survey was conducted to assess the need of statistical data analysis consultancy center in the university premises. Data is collected from those students and faculty members who visited department to attend the event (Data Analysis Consultancy Desk) that was organized by LISA-LCWU in March, 2022 as a part of sustainability experiment. Total sample comprised of 138 respondents, including 43.5% teaching faculty members and 56.5% students. Majority of respondents (93.5%) are found in favor of having statistical data analysis consultancy center (stat lab). It has been observed that respondents enrolled in different programs wants specific forum/platform like stat labs that can facilitates them to address the different issues they face in handling the data and drawing conclusions (Fig. 4). Considerable majority of the researchers wants the consultant to teach them how to perform statistical analysis. Most popular software, domain experts mentioned to use for data analysis is SPSS. It has been also observed that respondents are willing to give due credit to collaborator in the form of co-authorship and cash payments (Fig. 4; Table 3). Respondents (18.3%) need guidance from the collaborators in the selection of appropriate statistical method according to their research objectives. Majority of researchers (24.7%) mentioned that they need help in the interpretations of results obtained after application of statistical techniques.
